{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/stage-a-reader-brief.md clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/dryrun9/packet.json'","aggregated_output":"# Stage A reading form: is each answer a sound judged question for its thesis, or a justified refusal? (read-only)\n\nYou are an independent reader. Do not edit files, run model calls or start runs. Do not read any other reader's answers.\n\n## What you are reading\n\nThe packet you are given holds a list of items. Each item is one research topic (\"thesis\") a system opened\nwhile reading one news article, with a proposed **judged question** for it:\n- `thesis`: the fields the system wrote when it opened the topic: `description` (the topic's wording), `outcome` (what is tracked),\n  `period`, `opens_as`, `settled_by`;\n- `article`: the opening article's publication date, title and full text;\n- `ladder_as_the_judge_is_shown_it`: the proposed judged question exactly as a later judge will see it: its `object` (the company's\n  ticker NVDA, or a theme id), `kind`, `question`, `year`, `due_day` and its `rungs` (each a label and a condition; exactly one rung\n  is meant to hold on the due day). Or `no_ladder` with a reason: the step declined to write a question;\n- `other_fields`: what the step recorded beside the ladder and the judge does not see: `not_judged` (parts of the topic's wording\n  the question leaves out, with why), `reference` (what the article says the market expects, quoted), `favourable_end`,\n  `due_day_basis`.\n\nSome items are sound and some carry a fault. Judge each on its own against its thesis and its article.\n\n## The rules a judged question must meet\n\n- One judged question asks **one** figure for a named period or **one** event: the one the thesis's `outcome` names. Every other\n  part of the thesis's wording that the question leaves out (a second figure or event, a condition, a comparison) must be listed\n  in `not_judged`.\n- A yes/no event has two rungs, Yes and No; an event with more states, or a figure, has five. Exactly one rung holds for every\n  possible outcome: no overlap, no gap.\n- A question about the company's revenue, profit, share, product progress or its own obligations is the company's (object NVDA,\n  kind asset). A question about what happens in the world (licensing, aggregate spending, a policy) is a theme's.\n- A company's five-rung ladder runs from Strongly bullish to Strongly bearish, meaning good or bad for the company's business.\n- The reference is what the market expects for the question when it opens: a consensus, the company's guidance, a stated plan or\n  deadline. When the article states it as a number, the `reference` field carries that number and a figure's middle rung holds it.\n  When the article states it in words alone, the field carries the words and no number, and the ranges are the step's own\n  estimate.\n- The due day is when the question can be resolved: a figure's publication date; for an event, the date its outcome is assessed. Where\n  the thesis or the article states the day a figure is published, that day is right; where neither does, a plausible reporting\n  date after the period ends is right.\n- A company's figure for a quarter or a half-year is never a judged question: the step must decline it. A ladder written for\n  one is wrong even when it asks exactly what the thesis names (mark `Y`). An annual figure that only names quarterly reports as\n  the material that settles it is not such a case.\n- A step may decline (`no_ladder`) only in the six cases its instructions allow: the thesis has no main figure or event (its\n  outcome names several things and none is the main one); nothing in it can be checked on a date; it is the company's figure for a\n  quarter or a half-year; it is a figure for a year that had already ended on the article's day; it is a figure for a year beyond\n  next year, unless the thesis's `opens_as` is binding_obligation; or the question belongs to another company, or to a matter that\n  none of the listed themes covers (the listed themes are given with the packet). Declining for any other reason, or when the case\n  named does not truly apply, is not justified.\n\n## What to return\n\nOne JSON object per item, one per line, in item order, as your final message: no prose before or after, no code fence. Fields:\n\n| field | values | the mark |\n|---|---|---|\n| `item` | the item number | |\n| `Q` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | the judged question asks the thing the thesis's `outcome` names (`n/a` for a `no_ladder`) |\n| `O` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | the object is the question's own company or the right theme |\n| `R` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | exactly one rung holds for every outcome; for a yes/no, the Yes condition is the event happening and the No condition its complement |\n| `D` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | the due day follows the rule for its kind. A figure: a day by which the figure can be expected to have been published, after its period ends (the day the thesis or the article states, or, where neither states one, a plausible reporting date). An event: the date the thesis or the article gives for assessing it, or the last day of the period it names, or the company's fiscal year-end for a pending regulatory decision with no date. It fails when the day contradicts a date the thesis or the article gives, falls before the figure's period ends, or, for an event, is a date none of these gives |\n| `X` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | where the article states what the market expects for this quantity or event, the ladder places it rightly (a figure: the stated number lies in the middle rung; an expectation in words alone cannot be placed and holds); where the article states none, it holds unless the ladder claims one |\n| `F` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | for a five-rung ladder about the company only: the direction is defensible (which end is bullish, or the labels of the states); `n/a` for a yes/no ladder and for a theme |\n| `Y` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | for a figure only: the year and the unit are the question's, and the figure is a whole year's. A company's figure for a quarter or a half-year fails, whatever the thesis asks |\n| `G` | `holds`, `fails`, `not_assessable`, `n/a` | for a figure, always one of the first three: where the article gives any figure for this quantity, `holds` when an analyst would accept the ranges as a fair division of the outcomes around it and `fails` when not; `not_assessable` when the article gives none. `n/a` only for an event's ladder and for a `no_ladder` |\n| `L` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | every other part of the thesis's wording that the question leaves out (a second figure or event, a condition, a comparison) is listed in `not_judged`; a wording that asks nothing else holds with an empty list |\n| `B` | a list | exactly one entry for each part listed in `not_judged`, in its order: `\"bet\"` when an analyst would hold a separate view on it, `\"not_a_bet\"` when it is a detail of the judged question; `[]` when nothing is listed and for a `no_ladder` |\n| `XR` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | the `reference` field quotes what the article states the market expects; it carries the number when the article states one, and no number the article does not state; it is null only when the article states no expectation |\n| `N` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | for a `no_ladder` only: the refusal is justified by one of the allowed cases |\n| `W` | a string | any other fault that would mislead a reader of this judged question, in a short sentence; the empty string `\"\"` when there is none. The field is always present |\n| `why` | a string | one sentence giving the reason for every `fails` and for a non-empty `W`, naming the words or the figure; it may be empty only when no mark fails and `W` is empty |\n\nRead each item's article before answering it. Judge only what is in the item.\n[\n {\n  \"item\": 1,\n  \"thesis\": {\n   \"description\": \"What revenue will GreenCart report for fiscal 2027 after lifting its outlook?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"GreenCart's fiscal 2027 revenue, against its guidance of about $17.2 billion.\",\n   \"period\": \"Fiscal 2027, the year ending 30 January 2027; published in mid-March 2027.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"product_node\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"GreenCart's quarterly earnings releases and its annual report for fiscal 2027.\"\n  },\n  \"article\": {\n   \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-10\",\n   \"publisher\": \"retailwire.example\",\n   \"title\": \"GreenCart lifts full-year revenue outlook\",\n   \"text\": \"GreenCart Grocers (GRCR) raised its full-year outlook on Thursday, saying it now expects revenue of about $17.2 billion for fiscal 2027, the year ending 30 January 2027, up from the $16.8 billion it guided in March. New stores in the south-west opened ahead of plan. Investors will get updates with the quarterly reports in August and November; the full-year result is published with the fourth-quarter earnings release in mid-March 2027. Shares rose 3%.\"\n  },\n  \"ladder_as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n   \"object\": \"GRCR\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\",\n   \"question\": \"What revenue will GreenCart report for FY2027, the year ending 30 January 2027, in its fourth-quarter earnings release and annual report?\",\n   \"year\": \"FY2027\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-03-15\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"18,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 17,500,000,000 USD to below 18,000,000,000 USD\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 16,900,000,000 USD to below 17,500,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \\\"it now expects revenue of about $17.2 billion for fiscal 2027\\\")\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 16,400,000,000 USD to below 16,900,000,000 USD\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"below 16,400,000,000 USD\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"other_fields\": {\n   \"not_judged\": [],\n   \"reference\": {\n    \"words\": \"it now expects revenue of about $17.2 billion for fiscal 2027\",\n    \"value\": 17200000000\n   },\n   \"favourable_end\": \"higher\",\n   \"favourable_why\": \"Higher revenue is good for the grocer's business.\",\n   \"due_day_basis\": \"expected_publication\"\n  }\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 2,\n  \"thesis\": {\n   \"description\": \"What revenue will GreenCart report for the third quarter of fiscal 2027, after guiding below forecasts?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"GreenCart's third-quarter fiscal 2027 revenue, against its guidance of about $4.1 billion.\",\n   \"period\": \"The third quarter of fiscal 2027 (August to October 2026); results due late November 2026.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"product_node\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"GreenCart's third-quarter earnings release.\"\n  },\n  \"article\": {\n   \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-10\",\n   \"publisher\": \"retailwire.example\",\n   \"title\": \"GreenCart guides third-quarter sales below forecasts\",\n   \"text\": \"GreenCart Grocers (GRCR) said on Thursday it expects third-quarter revenue of about $4.1 billion, below the $4.3 billion analysts had forecast, as price cuts across its fresh-food ranges weigh on sales. The grocer's fiscal 2027 runs to 30 January 2027; its third quarter covers August to October 2026 and the results are due in late November. Chief financial officer Dana Whitlow said shoppers were trading down to own-label goods faster than the company had planned. Shares fell 4% in early trading. GreenCart did not change its outlook for the full year.\"\n  },\n  \"ladder_as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n   \"object\": \"GRCR\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\",\n   \"question\": \"What revenue will GreenCart report for the third quarter of FY2027 (August to October 2026) in its third-quarter earnings release?\",\n   \"year\": \"FY2027\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2026-11-30\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"4,500,000,000 USD or more\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 4,250,000,000 USD to below 4,500,000,000 USD\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 3,950,000,000 USD to below 4,250,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \\\"it expects third-quarter revenue of about $4.1 billion\\\")\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 3,700,000,000 USD to below 3,950,000,000 USD\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"below 3,700,000,000 USD\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"other_fields\": {\n   \"not_judged\": [],\n   \"reference\": {\n    \"words\": \"it expects third-quarter revenue of about $4.1 billion\",\n    \"value\": 4100000000\n   },\n   \"favourable_end\": \"higher\",\n   \"favourable_why\": \"Higher revenue is good for the grocer's business.\",\n   \"due_day_basis\": \"expected_publication\"\n  }\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 3,\n  \"thesis\": {\n   \"description\": \"What revenue will GreenCart report for the third quarter of fiscal 2027, after guiding below forecasts?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"GreenCart's third-quarter fiscal 2027 revenue, against its guidance of about $4.1 billion.\",\n   \"period\": \"The third quarter of fiscal 2027 (August to October 2026); results due late November 2026.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"product_node\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"GreenCart's third-quarter earnings release.\"\n  },\n  \"article\": {\n   \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-10\",\n   \"publisher\": \"retailwire.example\",\n   \"title\": \"GreenCart guides third-quarter sales below forecasts\",\n   \"text\": \"GreenCart Grocers (GRCR) said on Thursday it expects third-quarter revenue of about $4.1 billion, below the $4.3 billion analysts had forecast, as price cuts across its fresh-food ranges weigh on sales. The grocer's fiscal 2027 runs to 30 January 2027; its third quarter covers August to October 2026 and the results are due in late November. Chief financial officer Dana Whitlow said shoppers were trading down to own-label goods faster than the company had planned. Shares fell 4% in early trading. GreenCart did not change its outlook for the full year.\"\n  },\n  \"ladder_as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n   \"no_ladder\": \"The figure is the company's figure for a quarter, which is evidence to a yearly question.\"\n  },\n  \"other_fields\": {\n   \"not_judged\": null,\n   \"reference\": null,\n   \"favourable_end\": null,\n   \"favourable_why\": null,\n   \"due_day_basis\": null\n  }\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 4,\n  \"thesis\": {\n   \"description\": \"What operating profit will GreenCart report for the second half of fiscal 2027, given wage and price pressure?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"GreenCart's operating profit for the second half of fiscal 2027, against its guidance of about $310 million.\",\n   \"period\": \"The second half of fiscal 2027 (August 2026 to January 2027); full-year results in mid-March 2027.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"product_node\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"GreenCart's full-year results release, which gives the second half.\"\n  },\n  \"article\": {\n   \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-10\",\n   \"publisher\": \"retailwire.example\",\n   \"title\": \"GreenCart sees second-half profit of about $310 million\",\n   \"text\": \"GreenCart Grocers (GRCR) said it expects operating profit of about $310 million for the second half of fiscal 2027, the six months from August 2026 to January 2027, as wage increases and price cuts squeeze margins. Analysts polled before the update had expected about $340 million. The grocer's fiscal year ends on 30 January 2027 and it publishes its full-year results in mid-March. Chief executive Mara Olsen said the company would protect prices on staples through the holiday season.\"\n  },\n  \"ladder_as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n   \"object\": \"GRCR\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\",\n   \"question\": \"What operating profit will GreenCart report for the second half of FY2027 (August 2026 to January 2027) in its full-year results release?\",\n   \"year\": \"FY2027\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-03-15\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"370,000,000 USD or more\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 330,000,000 USD to below 370,000,000 USD\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 290,000,000 USD to below 330,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \\\"it expects operating profit of about $310 million for the second half of fiscal 2027\\\")\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 250,000,000 USD to below 290,000,000 USD\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"below 250,000,000 USD\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"other_fields\": {\n   \"not_judged\": [],\n   \"reference\": {\n    \"words\": \"it expects operating profit of about $310 million for the second half of fiscal 2027\",\n    \"value\": 310000000\n   },\n   \"favourable_end\": \"higher\",\n   \"favourable_why\": \"Higher operating profit is good for the grocer's business.\",\n   \"due_day_basis\": \"expected_publication\"\n  }\n }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"item\":1,\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"holds\",\"Y\":\"holds\",\"G\":\"holds\",\"L\":\"holds\",\"B\":[],\"XR\":\"holds\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"\"}\n{\"item\":2,\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"holds\",\"Y\":\"fails\",\"G\":\"holds\",\"L\":\"holds\",\"B\":[],\"XR\":\"holds\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"GreenCart's third-quarter revenue is a company figure for a quarter, so it cannot be a judged question.\"}\n{\"item\":3,\"Q\":\"n/a\",\"O\":\"n/a\",\"R\":\"n/a\",\"D\":\"n/a\",\"X\":\"n/a\",\"F\":\"n/a\",\"Y\":\"n/a\",\"G\":\"n/a\",\"L\":\"n/a\",\"B\":[],\"XR\":\"n/a\",\"N\":\"holds\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"\"}\n{\"item\":4,\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"holds\",\"Y\":\"fails\",\"G\":\"holds\",\"L\":\"holds\",\"B\":[],\"XR\":\"holds\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"GreenCart's second-half operating profit is a company figure for a half-year, so it cannot be a judged question.\"}"}}
